  "command": "source 'scripts/env.sh' && CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PHP_WASM_MAX_LOAD='20' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PHP_WASM_MODES='full,result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PHP_WASM_OUTPUT='build/vo1507-nested-record-php-wasm/records' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PHP_WASM_ROUTES='ordinary,reviewed' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PHP_WASM_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_TEST_PHP_COPIED_RUNTIME='build/nested-checked-record-php-wasm-input/php-wasm-runtime' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' 'node' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' 'tests/helpers/nested-checked-record-php-wasm-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Composer API, npm component and npm shared-runtime archives. Author and build roots are removed before offline installation and physical relocation; unchanged weak and strict callers run in eight Node embedded/Composer and four Chromium bundled startup/lazy contexts, giving twelve executions per selection. The full API checks direct and repeated parameters, Array, List, Option, Product, both Except branches, Holder.packet and the active ChoicePacket.value field, including exact per-site constructors, normalization, complete rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Checked-record PHP-Wasm acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited checked records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete Composer API, npm component and npm shared-runtime archives from two author roots, remove author and build roots, install offline, physically relocate each installation, and run unchanged weak and strict callers in eight Node and four Chromium contexts. The runs use wasm32 PHP 8.4.1, Node 22.23.2 and Chromium 152.0.7977.75 on Linux x64 with 32-bit machine words and a recorded 20.0 host-load admission ceiling. The archive retains complete packages, receipts, deployment callers, execution records and both producer and verifier source closures. Consumer PHP source remains required at runtime. The prepared PHP-Wasm runtime and browser remain trusted inputs; hosted acceptance remains assigned to the dedicated workflow. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured.",
